                <pb facs="0653" n="627" xml:id="pg627"/>

                <head>280. Telegram From Michael V. Forrestal of the National Security Council Staff
                    to the President, at Hyannis Port, Massachusetts<anchor n="1" xml:id="d280-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1963-08-24T16:50:00-04:00">August 24, 1963, 4:50
                            p.m.</date></hi></dateline></opener>
                <p>CAP 63460. Please pass following to President “eyes only”. Harriman, Hilsman and
                    Forrestal have drafted following telegram to Saigon and CINCPAC. Substance
                    generally agreed to by Admiral Felt and clearances being obtained, from Ball and
                    Defense. Since situation in Saigon may not remain fluid for long, Department
                    believes desirable transmit this message tonight. Ambassador Lodge agrees with
                    assessment that Nhu in control but does not know whether military would act
                    against him. Lodge recommends wait and see. Harriman, Hilsman and I favor taking
                    this action now. Will advise you reactions Ball and Defense, but suggest you let
                    me know if you wish comment or holdup action. Begin text draft cable:<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d280-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d280-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d280-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Vietnam Country Series
                    8/24/63-8/31/63, State Cables. Top Secret; Eyes Only. A note on the source text
                    in Clifton’s hand reads: P[resident]—as discussed with Secretary Ball.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d280-f2" n="2" xml:id="d280-f2-content">
                <p>No draft telegram was attached, but the reference is to a draft of telegram 243,
                        <ref target="#d281">Document 281</ref>. That draft is filed immediately
                    after this telegram in the Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Vietnam
                    Country Series, 8/24/63-8/31/63, State Cables. See <ref target="#d281-f8"
                        >footnote 8, Document 281</ref>, for the difference between the draft and
                    the final version.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
